title: DCRat Delivery via Brotli-Named DLL Sideloading
id: 9e620900-68f4-4ded-aa3b-3ba948509f28
status: experimental
description: Detects creation of libbrotlidec.dll or libbrotlienc.dll in non-standard directories, consistent with the DCRat (DarkCrystal RAT) delivery chain documented by Trellix that HTML-smuggles a password-protected 7z archive through an SVG attachment and sideloads attacker-controlled Brotli-named DLLs next to a decoy executable.
references:
    - https://gbhackers.com/malicious-svg-reconstructs-dcrat-archive-entirely-inside-victims-browser/
    - https://cyberpress.org/dcrat-hides-inside-windows/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/08/15
tags:
    - attack.t1027
    - attack.t1574
logsource:
    category: file_event
    product: windows
detection:
    selection:
        TargetFilename|endswith:
            - '\libbrotlidec.dll'
            - '\libbrotlienc.dll'
    filter_standard:
        TargetFilename|startswith:
            - 'C:\Program Files\'
            - 'C:\Program Files (x86)\'
            - 'C:\Windows\'
            - 'C:\ProgramData\'
    condition: selection and not filter_standard
falsepositives:
    - Applications that legitimately bundle Brotli libraries and install them to user-writable or app-local directories
    - Software updaters staging Brotli DLLs during installation
level: high
